    "updated_at": "2026-11-25T01:02:13Z",
    "body": "The red runs are runner setup failures, not code failures. Each failure ran on one of two new runners. The commits that ran on the older runners are green (`02d05bc1c`, `d796974b5`, `33597a2fb`, `785c31cf8`).\n\n| Commit | Runner | Error |\n|---|---|---|\n| `f2a2b8dee`, `808c540a9` | `FlamingFire_System` | `cargo: command not found` (exit 127) in \"Batch gate tier\"; the report step then gives `gh: command not found`. The runner service PATH has no `~/.cargo/bin` and no `gh`. |\n| `371416c98` | `HotTamale` | `failed to create directory /usr/local/cargo/git/db/solidcore-...: Permission denied (os error 13)`. The runner user cannot write `CARGO_HOME` (`/usr/local/cargo`). |\n\nPossible fixes:\n- `FlamingFire_System`: put `~/.cargo/bin` on the runner service PATH (the runner's `.path` file or `.env`), install `gh`, and restart the service.\n- `HotTamale`: give the runner user its own writable `CARGO_HOME` (for example `CARGO_HOME=/home/docker/.cargo` in the runner's `.env`), or make `/usr/local/cargo` writable by that user.\n\nUntil they are fixed, these runners turn each commit they take red. The affected commits can be run again on a working runner.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
